  "notes": [
    "**Salir** is irregular in present and future/conditional",
    "Present: irregular \"yo\" form (salgo), otherwise regular -IR endings",
    "Preterite: regular -IR conjugation",
    "Imperfect: regular -IR pattern",
    "Pretérito Perfecto: regular past participle **salido**",
    "Future: irregular stem \"saldr-\" (not \"salir-\")",
    "Condicional: irregular stem \"saldr-\" + conditional endings",
    "Multiple meanings: to leave, to go out, to exit, to come out",
    "Common usage: *salir de casa* (to leave home), *salir con amigos* (to go out with friends), *salir bien* (to turn out well)",
    "Opposite: **entrar** (to enter)",
    "Expression: *salir adelante* (to get ahead, to succeed)"
  ],
